Subject: monitor mode, the position and the levels on standard output

-M writes the state of the player on standard output, one line each, for a
program that shows it. It works with -t, -l and alone, and -C includes it. Without
-M or -C nothing is written, as before.

  ready CHANNELS FILE-RATE SERVER-RATE FRAMES   once, when the ports exist
  pos FRAME STATE                               when it changes
                                                (STATE: paused, playing or ended)
  lev PEAK PEAK ...                             about thirty times a second while
                                                there is sound, and once more with
                                                the zeros

Nothing is said while nothing changes: a paused player is silent on its output.

The levels are the highest sample of each channel since the last line, as the
program sends it out (1.0 is full scale, -g counted), measured in the process
thread and taken by the thread that writes the lines, without a lock. The
position is a frame of the file, and in transport mode it follows the transport:
a locate sets it, and the state is paused while the transport is stopped.
With -l the position goes back to the start of the file at each turn.
